<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Linares</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Linares is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaen">Jaén</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, near the ruins of the ancient Iberian city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castulo">Castulo</a>. Its lead and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines, worked since antiquity, made it one of the world's leading lead producers in the 19th century. It is the birthplace of the guitarist Andrés <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segovia">Segovia</a>.</p></div>
